{"id":"417187329","kind":"article","title":"间隔重复可能是培养或改变习惯的有用工具","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z249N76MhdBzDfrwMnqP6jEsTv6Z8u2kJrp8"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"间隔重复 & 注意力管理","date":"2021-10-05","updated":"2024-05-18","votes":13,"comment_count":4,"minutes":2,"chars":864,"keywords":["间隔重复","习惯养成","决策","元认知"],"summary":"作者建议把间隔重复卡片用于练习一种决策习惯：遇到选项难以排序、分析陷入僵局时，练习寻找新的评估标准或承认信息不足；也可用具体情境卡反复演练这一反应。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/417187329","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"参考文献"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"NZaw5kBL\">想象一下，你读了一篇文章，其中提出了这样的建议：</p><blockquote data-pid=\"42PiUyRY\">行动时难以抉择各种选项的优先级，到头来白费功夫？想用长长的利弊表来解决的话，如果其中各种因素本身不够有决定性也无济于事。要么开辟一条新路，或者确定更有力的评估，要么承认目前做不出足够明智的选择。</blockquote><p data-pid=\"CGXZ3V6p\">你可以用<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4eXdSMJFv2qVGXSUEKH4vdcHBrLHcFY1ZGfC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>来记忆文章中的片段，但你也可以用这个系统来把这个习惯「安装」在你的头脑中。下面一些样例问题可供尝试：</p><blockquote data-pid=\"-UHscIRo\">问：回忆出一个时候你在一直白费功夫，试图确定各种选择的优先次序。（对于这个问题，再想出一种之前没想过的情况）<br/>答：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z249N76MhdBzDfrwMnqP6jEsTv6Z8u2kJrp8\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">空白</a><br/><br/>问：想象一下，你发现自己陷入优先次序不明确的困境后，可能会采取的具体步骤，这些步骤不算常规。（写出你以前没有想到过的步骤）<br/>答：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z249N76MhdBzDfrwMnqP6jEsTv6Z8u2kJrp8\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">空白</a><br/><br/>问：设想一种特定的情况，在这种情况下，你很难通过找到一个决定性的因素来摆脱优先次序的泥潭。（写一个你以前没有想过的情况）<br/>答：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z249N76MhdBzDfrwMnqP6jEsTv6Z8u2kJrp8\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">空白</a></blockquote><p data-pid=\"hS2EXlu-\">在你回答过几次这种关于特定习惯的卡片后，做出更具体的卡片来强化这个习惯往往会有帮助。例如(<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://twitter.com/kanjun/status/1278501271226298368\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">来自 Kanjun，2020-07-01</a>)：「当我早上拿起牙刷时…」「…拿起我的手机，打开 Anki。」</p><p data-pid=\"cxbx-bRE\">这是一个<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2gqazXUkf9qyFjMQg4W3dw6yegnAJszvDywN\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可使用间隔重复系统对注意力进行编程</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>的例子。</p><hr/><h2 id=\"sec-1\">参考文献</h2><p data-pid=\"3_h0wMo-\">与 Florent Crivello 的对话，2019-11-17</p><p data-pid=\"my3EZI_W\">相关信息来自 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Alexey_Guzey\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Alexey Guzey</a>：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://guzey.com/things/software/anki/#instilling-novel-thought-patterns-with-anki\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">用 Anki 灌输新的思维模式并使你的长期记忆负责 - Alexey Guzey</a></p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"Vc7Pgf7n\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"501187896\" href=\"#/post/501187896\">§收件箱与注意力管理</a></li><li data-pid=\"s0jyjoeP\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"698476935\" href=\"#/post/698476935\">§赋能环境、游戏和《启蒙琼林》</a></li><li data-pid=\"leFuDRF7\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"414293765\" href=\"#/post/414293765\">可使用间隔重复系统对注意力编程</a></li><li data-pid=\"zY4Pf7wb\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"412311494\" href=\"#/post/412311494\">间隔重复记忆系统可用于促进应用、综合和创造</a></li><li data-pid=\"ZOM11AHk\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"413535553\" href=\"#/post/413535553\">间隔重复记忆系统的特殊应用</a></li><li data-pid=\"6Q04w8kw\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"443011535\" href=\"#/post/443011535\">间隔重复系统与教义问答</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-3\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"EbqDYas3\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"hEKlVZON\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z249N76MhdBzDfrwMnqP6jEsTv6Z8u2kJrp8\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Spaced repetition may be a helpful tool to develop or change habits</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404257681\" href=\"#/post/404257681\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 可使用间隔重复系统对注意力编程 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"414293765\" href=\"#/post/414293765\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"415857130","title":"间隔重复对于逐步完善灵光一闪可能有用","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":29,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"417555450","title":"没有源源不断的新卡片，间隔重复的复习环节常常变得枯燥而脱节","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":10,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"501187896","title":"§收件箱与注意力管理","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":27,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"698476935","title":"§赋能环境、游戏和《启蒙琼林》","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":9,"minutes":6,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"414293765","title":"可使用间隔重复系统对注意力编程","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":24,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"1925894724595724883","title":"你的眼睛应该往哪儿放？浅谈玩电子游戏对做科研的启示。","author":"radimentary","votes":173,"minutes":18,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「元认知」· radimentary"}],"rec_answers":[]}